    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/10267": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Music - UT Southern",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Pulaski, TN, United States The department of Humanities and Social Sciences has periodic openings for part-time, adjunct faculty to teach on site or online in the Fine Arts: Music program. The department of Humanities and Social Sciences has periodic openings for part-time, adjunct faculty to teach on site or online in the Fine Arts: Music program. The primary responsibility will be teaching basic to advanced piano classes, individual applied music lessons in piano or other instruments, and upper-level music courses as needed in theory, music tech, composition, and music history. There may be opportunities for piano accompaniment as well. As part of our commitment to academic excellence, we are building a pool of skilled instructors who can contribute to students’ success through engaging and effective teaching. Applications from candidates available to teach on campus will be prioritized. Position Overview: Adjunct instructors in Fine Arts: Music will primarily teach piano-based classes and lessons. There may be opportunities to teach upper-level music courses and to accompany ensembles. Courses may be offered face-to-face or online, though face-to-face is preferred. The principal responsibility of the position is teaching undergraduate students. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without need now or in the future for sponsorship for employment visa status. Qualifications: Master's degree in Music with a specialty in piano, or a related field. Demonstrated piano proficiency. Proven record of quality instruction. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching college-level courses. Experience with learning management systems (LMS) such as Canvas. To apply, please submit 1) a cover letter addressing interest in and qualifications for the role, 2) a CV/resume, and 3) a list of three professional references. For full consideration, candidates should apply electronically through the University of Tennessee Careers site. Candidates who are able to provide on-site accompaniment may be asked to complete a brief audition with the Music Director. Teach courses on-campus or online as assigned. Accompany ensembles and other musical applications, depending on need. Musical applications may include ensemble accompaniment, voice studio, piano lessons, jury examinations, rehearsals, recitals, and university events. Work with the program director to ensure consistent and appropriate student learning. Utilize the University’s learning management system (Canvas) to assess student projects and record grades in a timely manner. Regularly check your email account. Respond to emails/messages in a timely manner. Complete all required reports, such as early grade alerts, midterm grades, and final grades."
    },
    "https://fa-ewlq-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/10184": {
      "title": "Adjunct Business Professor - UTS",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Pulaski, TN, United States The University is seeking an experienced and student-focused Adjunct Business Faculty member to teach undergraduate courses in business, management, information systems, entrepreneurship, and agricultural business. The successful candidate will bring relevant academic and/or professional experience and a commitment to providing students with engaging, practical, and career-focused learning experiences. The University is seeking an experienced and student-focused Adjunct Business Faculty member to teach undergraduate courses in business, management, information systems, entrepreneurship, and agricultural business. The successful candidate will bring relevant academic and/or professional experience and a commitment to providing students with engaging, practical, and career-focused learning experiences. The ideal candidate will be able to connect business concepts to real-world applications and demonstrate an ability to teach effectively in a traditional or online environment. Candidates with experience in information systems, management, entrepreneurship, agricultural business, leadership, organizational behavior, or related fields are encouraged to apply. The position offers an opportunity to contribute to student success while supporting the University's growing business and agricultural business programs. This is an adjunct, part-time position. Applications will be reviewed on an as-needed basis based on course availability, enrollment, and departmental needs. Submission of an application does not guarantee an immediate assignment or appointment. Because adjunct faculty are hired as instructional needs arise, applicants may not receive a response immediately and should understand that several weeks, months, or potentially longer, may pass before an opportunity becomes available. Qualified applicants may be contacted when a teaching need arises that aligns with their qualifications and experience. The University of Tennessee Southern (UT Southern) is a public university located in Pulaski, Tennessee, strategically positioned within the growing Nashville–Huntsville innovation corridor. As the newest campus in the University of Tennessee System — and the only public four-year institution between Chattanooga and Memphis — UT Southern offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact within a close-knit academic community while benefiting from the resources and reputation of a nationally recognized public university system. With more than 1,000 students, small class sizes, and a highly personalized academic environment, UT Southern combines the feel of a private college with the affordability of a public university. UT Southern’s Firehawks compete in the NAIA Southern States Athletic Conference and include nationally recognized championship programs. Faculty and staff at UT Southern play a direct role in shaping the future of a growing institution committed to academic excellence, student success, workforce development, and regional impact. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without need now or in the future for sponsorship for employment visa status. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Business or related discipline, or a master’s degree with 18 graduate credit hours in the teaching discipline. Preferred Qualifications: College-level teaching experience preferred. Professional experience in business, management, information systems, entrepreneurship, agriculture, or a related field is preferred. Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate business concepts and engage students in applied, experiential learning. Experience teaching in online, hybrid, or technology-enhanced learning environments preferred. Commitment to student success, timely communication, and providing meaningful feedback to students. Ability to use learning management systems and common instructional technologies effectively. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, program coordinators, and department leadership. Candidates with expertise in agricultural business, entrepreneurship, management information systems, leadership, or organizational behavior are particularly encouraged to apply. Please submit a cover letter that explains your interest in the position and highlights your qualifications for the role, and a current CV as part of your application. Teach assigned undergraduate business courses in accordance with University and department expectations. Prepare and deliver engaging, student-centered instruction in traditional and/or online formats. Maintain regular virtual office hours and provide timely communication and support to students. Evaluate student work and provide timely, constructive feedback that supports student learning and success. Maintain accurate and timely course records, including grades, attendance/participation, and other required documentation. Use the University's learning management system and other instructional technologies effectively. Incorporate current industry practices, real-world applications, and relevant examples into instruction when appropriate. Participate in required faculty meetings, training, professional development, and departmental activities as requested. Communicate regularly with the department head and/or program coordinator regarding course needs, student concerns, and other academic matters. Support the University's commitment to student success, academic quality, and a collaborative learning environment."
    }
